# mgarmory.msg - the armory door in the Sheriff's house (mgarmory.ssl).
# 100-102 look, 110-115 use, 120-131 being caught, 140-144 the lock.
# One entry per line; no braces in comments.

{100}{}{You see a steel-banded door with a lock the size of a fist.}
{101}{}{Plate steel riveted over planks, hinges on the inside. Somebody did not want this opened by anyone who has to ask.}
{102}{}{The lock hangs open. It looks faintly embarrassed.}

{110}{}{The door is locked. It does not rattle. It does not even shift.}
{113}{}{The lock is already open.}
{114}{}{The lock is all springs and steel. There is nothing in it for an electronic pick to argue with.}
{115}{}{You find no traps. The sheriff trusts the lock, and the lock has earned it.}

# Floating over the witness: 120, 121 Simms; 122, 123 Harden.
{120}{}{Step away from that door. You get one warning in this town. That was it.}
{121}{}{I told you once.}
{122}{}{Hey! Those are my dad's! I'm telling!}
{123}{}{THIEF! THE STRANGER'S AT THE GUNS AGAIN!}
{130}{}{You have been seen. You take your hands off the lock and try to look like someone admiring the carpentry. You will not be warned twice.}
{131}{}{Caught at the sheriff's lock a second time. The shout crosses Megaton faster than you can.}

{140}{}{The last tumbler gives with a click you feel in your teeth. The sheriff's armory is open.}
{141}{}{Pin by pin the lock lets you in, and at the last one it changes its mind. You are close. A finer set of picks, or steadier fingers, would do it.}
{142}{}{You work at the lock until your fingers cramp. It ignores you. This one is beyond you, for now.}
{143}{}{You prod at the keyhole with what you have. Without a set of picks you might as well whistle at it.}
{144}{}{Pin by pin the lock lets you in, and at the last one it changes its mind. Your picks are good enough. Your fingers are not, yet.}
